  "nl_text": "The database schema named 'rschema_0410' consists of 8 tables.\nThe 'User_Information' table is used to store user-related information. It includes columns for 'Password', 'Role', 'User_ID' (as the primary key), and 'Username'.\nThe 'Vehicle_Information' table stores information about the vehicles. It includes columns for 'Vehicle_Category', 'Vehicle_ID' (as the primary key), 'Vehicle_Name', 'Vehicle_Photo' (as a BLOB type for storing binary data), and 'Vehicle_Status'.\nThe 'Repair_Shop_Information' table contains information about the repair shops. It includes columns for 'Contact_Number', 'Contact_Person', 'Repair_Shop_ID' (as the primary key), and 'Shop_Name'.\nThe 'Announcement_Information' table stores information about announcements. It includes columns for 'Announcement_ID' (as the primary key), 'Content', 'Creation_Time', and 'Title'.\nThe 'Token_Information' table stores information about tokens. It includes columns for 'Creation_Time', 'Expiration_Time', 'Token_ID' (as the primary key), and 'Token_Value'.\nThe 'Vehicle_Maintenance' table is used to store information about vehicle maintenance. It includes columns for 'Is_Reviewed', 'Maintenance_Details', 'Maintenance_ID' (as the primary key), 'Maintenance_Time', 'Review_Reply', and 'Vehicle_ID' (as a foreign key referencing the 'Vehicle_Information' table).\nThe 'Vehicle_Trip' table stores information about vehicle trips. It includes columns for 'Trip_ID' (as the primary key), 'Trip_Remarks', 'Trip_Time', and 'Vehicle_ID' (as a foreign key referencing the 'Vehicle_Information' table).\nFinally, the 'Vehicle_Maintenance_Application' table is used to store applications for vehicle maintenance. It includes columns for 'Application_ID' (as the primary key), 'Application_Reason', 'Application_Time', 'Is_Reviewed', 'Review_Reply', and 'Vehicle_ID' (as a foreign key referencing the 'Vehicle_Information' table).",
  "gold_question": "The diagram depicts a vehicle management system. The main functions of the system may include:\n\n1. User management: including adding, modifying, deleting and querying user information.\n2. Vehicle information management: including adding, modifying, deleting and querying vehicle information.\n3. Vehicle maintenance management: including adding, modifying, deleting and querying maintenance records.\n4. Vehicle departure management: including adding, modifying, deleting and querying departure records.\n5. Vehicle maintenance application management: including submitting, reviewing and querying maintenance applications.\n6. Vehicle repair shop management: including adding, modifying, deleting and querying repair shop information.\n7. Announcement information management: including publishing, modifying, deleting and querying announcements.\n8. Token information management: including token generation, verification and expiration processing.\n\nThe corresponding database model is as follows:\n\n1. User information table: including fields such as user ID, user name, password, role, etc.\n\n2. Vehicle information table: including fields such as vehicle ID, vehicle name, vehicle photo, vehicle status, vehicle category, etc.\n3. Vehicle maintenance table: including fields such as maintenance ID, vehicle ID, maintenance time, maintenance details, whether to review, review reply, etc.\n4. Vehicle departure table: including fields such as departure ID, vehicle ID, departure time, departure notes, etc.\n5. Vehicle maintenance application form: including fields such as application ID, vehicle ID, application time, application reason, whether to review, review reply, etc.\n6. Repair shop information table: including fields such as repair shop ID, shop name, contact person, contact number, etc.\n7. Announcement information table: including fields such as announcement ID, title, content, creation time, etc.\n8. Token information table: including fields such as tokenID, token value, creation time, expiration time, etc.",
  "input_json": "/data/RSchema_ExpResults4/Experiment2/schema2text_deepseek/0410.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0410\nCREATE TABLE `user_information` (\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `username` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `password` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `role` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`user_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `vehicle_information` (\n  `vehicle_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `vehicle_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `vehicle_category` varchar(100) NOT NULL,\n  `vehicle_photo` blob DEFAULT NULL,\n  `vehicle_status` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`vehicle_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `repair_shop_information` (\n  `repair_shop_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `shop_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `contact_person` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `contact_number` varchar(15) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`repair_shop_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `announcement_information` (\n  `announcement_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `title` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `content` text NOT NULL,\n  `creation_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`announcement_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `token_information` (\n  `token_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `token_value` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `creation_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `expiration_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`token_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `vehicle_maintenance` (\n  `maintenance_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `maintenance_details` text NOT NULL,\n  `maintenance_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `is_reviewed` tinyint(1) NOT NULL,\n  `review_reply` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `vehicle_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`maintenance_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `vehicle_maintenance_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`vehicle_id`) REFERENCES `vehicle_information` (`vehicle_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `vehicle_trip` (\n  `trip_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `trip_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `trip_remarks` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `vehicle_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`trip_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `vehicle_trip_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`vehicle_id`) REFERENCES `vehicle_information` (`vehicle_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `vehicle_maintenance_application` (\n  `application_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `application_reason` text NOT NULL,\n  `application_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `is_reviewed` tinyint(1) NOT NULL,\n  `review_reply` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `vehicle_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`application_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `vehicle_maintenance_application_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`vehicle_id`) REFERENCES `vehicle_information` (`vehicle_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
